---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Resume Tips & Interview Prep - MNC Jobs">
	<main class="container">
		<header class="header">
			<div class="header-content">
				<h1>MNC Interview & Resume Tips</h1>
				<p>Master the skills needed to land your dream MNC job</p>
			</div>
		</header>

		<div class="content-wrapper">
			<section class="tips-section">
				<h2>Resume Writing Guide</h2>
				<div class="tips-content">
					<article class="tip-article">
						<h3>1. Use Action Verbs</h3>
						<p>Start bullet points with strong action verbs like "Developed", "Implemented", "Optimized", "Led", instead of "Worked on" or "Helped with".</p>
						<p><strong>Good:</strong> "Developed REST API that reduced response time by 40%"</p>
						<p><strong>Bad:</strong> "Worked on API development"</p>
					</article>

					<article class="tip-article">
						<h3>2. Tailor for Each Position</h3>
						<p>Read the job description carefully and include relevant keywords. ATS systems scan for specific skills and terms.</p>
						<p>Highlight: Programming languages, frameworks, tools, certifications mentioned in the job posting.</p>
					</article>

					<article class="tip-article">
						<h3>3. Format Matters</h3>
						<p>Use consistent formatting with standard fonts (Calibri, Arial, Times New Roman). Avoid:</p>
						<ul>
							<li>Graphics, images, tables</li>
							<li>Unusual fonts or colors</li>
							<li>Headers/footers with important info</li>
							<li>PDF with embedded fonts</li>
						</ul>
					</article>

					<article class="tip-article">
						<h3>4. Quantify Everything</h3>
						<p>Numbers make your achievements stand out:</p>
						<ul>
							<li>Project cost savings: "Reduced infrastructure costs by 35% ($50K/year)"</li>
							<li>Performance improvements: "Improved database query performance by 60%"</li>
							<li>User impact: "Served 100K+ daily active users"</li>
							<li>Timeline: "Delivered project 2 weeks ahead of schedule"</li>
						</ul>
					</article>

					<article class="tip-article">
						<h3>5. Education Section Tips</h3>
						<ul>
							<li>Include CGPA if 7.5 or higher</li>
							<li>List relevant coursework if you're a fresher</li>
							<li>Mention scholarships or honors</li>
							<li>Include graduation year (or expected)</li>
							<li>Add university location</li>
						</ul>
					</article>

					<article class="tip-article">
						<h3>6. Skills Section Strategy</h3>
						<p>Organize skills by category:</p>
						<ul>
							<li><strong>Languages:</strong> Java, Python, JavaScript, C++</li>
							<li><strong>Frameworks:</strong> Spring Boot, React, Django</li>
							<li><strong>Databases:</strong> MySQL, PostgreSQL, MongoDB</li>
							<li><strong>Tools:</strong> Git, Docker, Jenkins, AWS</li>
							<li><strong>Soft Skills:</strong> Leadership, Problem-solving, Communication</li>
						</ul>
					</article>

					<article class="tip-article">
						<h3>7. Common Mistakes to Avoid</h3>
						<ul>
							<li>❌ Spelling and grammar errors (use spell check!)</li>
							<li>❌ Lies about skills or experience</li>
							<li>❌ Too long (keep to 1-2 pages)</li>
							<li>❌ Irrelevant work experience</li>
							<li>❌ Missing contact information</li>
							<li>❌ Outdated or personal email addresses</li>
						</ul>
					</article>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="tips-section">
				<h2>Interview Preparation</h2>
				<div class="tips-content">
					<article class="tip-article">
						<h3>Before the Interview</h3>
						<ul>
							<li>Research the company: products, culture, recent news</li>
							<li>Understand the role: required skills, responsibilities</li>
							<li>Prepare your story: why you, why this role, career goals</li>
							<li>Practice common questions: "Tell me about yourself", "Why do you want to join?"</li>
							<li>Test your setup: internet, microphone, camera (for online interviews)</li>
							<li>Be 5 minutes early (for in-person or join 5 min early for video calls)</li>
						</ul>
					</article>

					<article class="tip-article">
						<h3>STAR Method for Behavioral Questions</h3>
						<p><strong>S</strong>ituation, <strong>T</strong>ask, <strong>A</strong>ction, <strong>R</strong>esult</p>
						<p>Example: "Tell me about a time you solved a difficult problem"</p>
						<ul>
							<li><strong>Situation:</strong> "In my internship at XYZ, we had a performance bottleneck..."</li>
							<li><strong>Task:</strong> "I was assigned to identify and fix the issue..."</li>
							<li><strong>Action:</strong> "I analyzed the code, found N+1 queries, and optimized them..."</li>
							<li><strong>Result:</strong> "Response time improved by 60%, affecting 10K+ users positively"</li>
						</ul>
					</article>

					<article class="tip-article">
						<h3>Technical Interview Tips</h3>
						<ul>
							<li>Clarify requirements before coding</li>
							<li>Think out loud - explain your approach</li>
							<li>Ask about edge cases and constraints</li>
							<li>Write clean, readable code</li>
							<li>Test your solution with examples</li>
							<li>Optimize if time permits</li>
							<li>If stuck, explain your thought process</li>
						</ul>
					</article>

					<article class="tip-article">
						<h3>Questions to Ask Interviewer</h3>
						<ul>
							<li>What does a typical day look like in this role?</li>
							<li>What are the main challenges this team faces?</li>
							<li>How is success measured in this position?</li>
							<li>What's the team structure and who would I report to?</li>
							<li>What are the growth opportunities?</li>
							<li>What's the tech stack and tools you use?</li>
						</ul>
					</article>

					<article class="tip-article">
						<h3>After the Interview</h3>
						<ul>
							<li>Send a thank you email within 24 hours</li>
							<li>Reiterate your interest and key points from discussion</li>
							<li>Keep it brief (2-3 paragraphs)</li>
							<li>Personalize: mention specific things you discussed</li>
							<li>Proofread carefully</li>
						</ul>
					</article>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="tips-section">
				<h2>MNC Salary Negotiation</h2>
				<div class="tips-content">
					<article class="tip-article">
						<h3>Know Your Worth</h3>
						<ul>
							<li>Research average salaries for your role/experience level</li>
							<li>Use sites like Levels.fyi, Glassdoor, AmbitionBox</li>
							<li>Factor in: location, company size, experience</li>
							<li>Base salary is just one component</li>
						</ul>
					</article>

					<article class="tip-article">
						<h3>Offer Components (Total Compensation)</h3>
						<ul>
							<li><strong>Base Salary:</strong> Fixed annual salary</li>
							<li><strong>Signing Bonus:</strong> One-time bonus upon joining</li>
							<li><strong>Annual Bonus:</strong> Performance-based bonus (typically 10-30%)</li>
							<li><strong>Stock Options:</strong> Equity/RSUs (if applicable)</li>
							<li><strong>Benefits:</strong> Health insurance, PF, gratuity</li>
							<li><strong>Perks:</strong> Flexible work, learning budget, relocation</li>
						</ul>
					</article>

					<article class="tip-article">
						<h3>Negotiation Tips</h3>
						<ul>
							<li>✅ Always negotiate - first offer is rarely the best</li>
							<li>✅ Get the offer in writing before discussing salary</li>
							<li>✅ Ask for 2-3 business days to consider</li>
							<li>✅ Research before responding with counter-offer</li>
							<li>✅ Be respectful and professional</li>
							<li>✅ Focus on value you bring, not personal needs</li>
							<li>✅ Negotiate everything - not just base salary</li>
						</ul>
					</article>
				</div>
			</section>
		</div>

		<div class="ad-space">
			<div class="placeholder">Advertisement</div>
		</div>
	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	:root {
		--primary: #0066cc;
		--secondary: #f0f4f9;
		--text-dark: #1a1a1a;
		--text-light: #666;
		--border: #ddd;
		--spacing: 1rem;
		--spacing-lg: 2rem;
		--spacing-xl: 3rem;
	}

	.container {
		max-width: 100%;
		margin: 0 auto;
	}

	.header {
		background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--primary) 0%, #0052a3 100%);
		color: white;
		padding: var(--spacing-xl) var(--spacing);
		text-align: center;
	}

	.header-content h1 {
		margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
		font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 2.5rem);
	}

	.header-content p {
		margin: 0;
		opacity: 0.9;
	}

	.content-wrapper {
		max-width: 1000px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: var(--spacing-xl) var(--spacing);
	}

	.tips-section {
		margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
	}

	.tips-section h2 {
		color: var(--primary);
		margin: var(--spacing-xl) 0 var(--spacing-lg);
		font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 3vw, 1.8rem);
		border-bottom: 2px solid var(--primary);
		padding-bottom: var(--spacing);
	}

	.tip-article {
		margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
		padding-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
	}

	.tip-article:last-child {
		border-bottom: none;
	}

	.tip-article h3 {
		color: var(--text-dark);
		margin: 0 0 var(--spacing) 0;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
	}

	.tip-article p {
		margin: 0 0 var(--spacing) 0;
		line-height: 1.8;
		color: var(--text-light);
	}

	.tip-article ul {
		margin: var(--spacing) 0;
		padding-left: 1.5rem;
		color: var(--text-light);
	}

	.tip-article li {
		margin: 0.5rem 0;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}

	.ad-space {
		background: var(--secondary);
		padding: var(--spacing);
		text-align: center;
		margin: var(--spacing-xl) 0;
	}

	.placeholder {
		color: var(--text-light);
		min-height: 100px;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		background: #f9f9f9;
		border: 1px dashed var(--border);
		border-radius: 4px;
	}

	@media (max-width: 768px) {
		.content-wrapper {
			padding: var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing);
		}
	}
</style>
